WEBVTT

00:00.190 --> 00:01.980
Before we start asking ChatGPT

00:01.840 --> 00:02.900
to help with real estate

00:02.800 --> 00:04.250
work, we need to give

00:04.110 --> 00:05.980
it a little basic context.

00:05.840 --> 00:08.020
If ChatGPT knows nothing about

00:07.880 --> 00:09.980
you, every new conversation starts

00:09.840 --> 00:10.870
like you're talking to a

00:10.730 --> 00:11.820
stranger.

00:11.680 --> 00:12.950
You can still get useful

00:12.860 --> 00:14.320
answers, but you're going to

00:14.180 --> 00:15.790
spend more time explaining what

00:15.650 --> 00:16.940
you do, who you work

00:16.800 --> 00:18.170
with, and how you want

00:18.030 --> 00:19.260
things written.

00:19.310 --> 00:21.490
Personalization gives ChatGPT a starting

00:21.460 --> 00:22.140
point.

00:22.000 --> 00:23.490
It helps it understand the

00:23.350 --> 00:25.000
basics of your role, your

00:24.860 --> 00:27.010
market, and your communication style.

00:27.790 --> 00:28.690
This is not where we

00:28.650 --> 00:30.720
build your entire business brain.

00:30.750 --> 00:32.030
We're just creating a clean

00:31.890 --> 00:33.520
foundation so the Assistant has

00:33.380 --> 00:35.190
useful context from the beginning.

00:35.303 --> 00:36.893
Let's open chat GPT settings

00:36.803 --> 00:38.433
and go to Personalization.

00:38.293 --> 00:39.473
The labels can move around

00:39.333 --> 00:40.663
a little as the product

00:40.523 --> 00:42.193
updates, but the goal stays

00:42.053 --> 00:42.913
the same.

00:42.813 --> 00:43.793
We're looking for the place

00:43.653 --> 00:44.893
where chat GPT lets you

00:44.893 --> 00:46.113
tell it who you are,

00:46.193 --> 00:47.283
what you do, and how

00:47.203 --> 00:48.483
you want it to communicate

00:48.343 --> 00:48.993
with you.

00:48.853 --> 00:50.193
As you go through these

00:50.053 --> 00:52.353
options, don't overthink every word.

00:52.213 --> 00:53.333
The point is to give

00:53.193 --> 00:55.073
chat GPT enough information to

00:54.933 --> 00:56.943
be helpful without turning this

00:56.803 --> 00:58.283
into a giant biography or

00:58.163 --> 00:58.673
a complicated

00:59.063 --> 01:00.113
technical project.

01:00.422 --> 01:02.142
For this example, we're using

01:02.222 --> 01:04.162
Steve Rogers, a synthetic real

01:04.022 --> 01:05.552
estate agent persona who is

01:05.582 --> 01:07.262
originally from New York and

01:07.132 --> 01:09.702
now lives in Jacksonville, Florida.

01:09.562 --> 01:11.652
Steve's current market is Jacksonville

01:11.512 --> 01:13.342
and the broader Northeast Florida

01:13.552 --> 01:13.932
area.

01:13.912 --> 01:15.782
That is useful context because

01:15.642 --> 01:17.222
it tells ChatGPT where Steve

01:17.082 --> 01:18.382
works and what kind of

01:18.242 --> 01:19.962
local real estate help should

01:19.822 --> 01:21.062
be most relevant.

01:21.182 --> 01:22.462
Start with the basics that

01:22.322 --> 01:23.352
are true most of the

01:23.212 --> 01:25.482
time, your preferred name, your

01:25.342 --> 01:27.902
occupation, your broad market, your

01:27.762 --> 01:29.492
specialties, and the kind of

01:29.462 --> 01:30.742
clients you serve.

01:30.602 --> 01:32.422
The more specific you are

01:32.372 --> 01:34.712
about your actual business, the

01:34.592 --> 01:36.502
less generic ChatGPT needs to

01:36.362 --> 01:38.202
be, but only include information

01:38.472 --> 01:39.822
that is appropriate to keep

01:39.732 --> 01:41.782
as general working context.

01:41.801 --> 01:42.231
Next, pay

01:42.551 --> 01:44.551
attention to communication preferences and

01:44.511 --> 01:46.651
any current personality or response-style

01:46.511 --> 01:47.771
options.

01:47.801 --> 01:48.231
For a real

01:48.551 --> 01:50.111
estate agent, a good starting

01:50.021 --> 01:52.741
point is usually clear, conversational,

01:52.601 --> 01:53.971
and educational.

01:54.001 --> 01:55.711
You might want direct answers,

01:55.571 --> 01:57.711
practical ideas, and language that

01:57.571 --> 01:59.111
sounds human instead of generic

01:58.971 --> 01:59.401
corporate

01:59.921 --> 02:00.271
marketing.

02:00.301 --> 02:01.341
What you do not need

02:01.201 --> 02:02.811
here is a 20-page life

02:02.671 --> 02:05.971
story, private client information, passwords,

02:06.221 --> 02:08.391
financial documents, or sensitive details

02:08.341 --> 02:09.661
about a current deal.

02:09.801 --> 02:10.231
Keep this

02:10.551 --> 02:11.041
simple.

02:10.901 --> 02:13.471
Personalization is basic context.

02:13.331 --> 02:14.591
It is not a filing

02:14.451 --> 02:15.756
cabinet, and it is not

02:15.616 --> 02:16.901
a replacement for the deeper

02:17.081 --> 02:18.321
knowledge files in AI Twin

02:18.181 --> 02:19.771
we're going to build later.

02:19.949 --> 02:21.059
If you're not sure what

02:20.919 --> 02:23.369
belongs in personalization, let ChatGPT

02:23.229 --> 02:24.619
interview you.

02:24.579 --> 02:25.519
We're going to use the

02:25.379 --> 02:27.009
lesson prompt that asks 10

02:27.149 --> 02:28.859
short questions about your market,

02:28.889 --> 02:32.349
business, clients, communication preferences, goals,

02:32.269 --> 02:33.169
and the kind of work

02:33.029 --> 02:34.409
you want AI helping you

02:34.269 --> 02:34.729
with.

02:34.709 --> 02:36.549
The important instruction is to

02:36.409 --> 02:37.609
ask one question at a

02:37.479 --> 02:38.139
time.

02:37.999 --> 02:38.559
That keeps the

02:38.929 --> 02:40.609
conversation useful instead of dumping

02:40.469 --> 02:42.209
a huge questionnaire on you.

02:42.069 --> 02:43.549
As Steve answers, you can

02:43.409 --> 02:43.579
see

02:43.969 --> 02:45.129
which details belong in the

02:45.089 --> 02:46.699
basic settings and which ideas

02:46.559 --> 02:47.829
should wait for a future

02:47.689 --> 02:49.369
project or your full Realtor

02:49.239 --> 02:50.119
AI Twin.

02:50.258 --> 02:52.048
When you're done, chat GPT

02:51.908 --> 02:53.688
should have a simple, useful

02:53.548 --> 02:54.628
starting point for how to

02:54.488 --> 02:55.568
work with you.

02:55.428 --> 02:56.958
It should understand that you're

02:56.818 --> 02:57.998
a real estate agent who

02:57.878 --> 02:59.728
you generally serve, where you

02:59.588 --> 03:00.628
work, and the kind of

03:00.488 --> 03:01.968
communication you prefer.

03:01.828 --> 03:03.568
That's the foundation.

03:03.428 --> 03:06.188
Later, we'll build much deeper

03:06.048 --> 03:07.978
context with your Realtor AI

03:07.838 --> 03:10.188
twin projects, knowledge files, and

03:10.048 --> 03:11.358
better prompts.

03:11.218 --> 03:12.758
For now, keep the settings

03:12.988 --> 03:14.708
clean, useful, and true to

03:14.568 --> 03:14.978
your real

03:15.448 --> 03:16.018
business.
